(KnowledgeDesk IT Support Runbook) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Version 1.0 - Internal Knowledge Base) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(Overview) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(This runbook helps IT support agents answer common employee support questions. It covers account access, VPN troubleshooting, laptop replacement, software installation, and escalation rules.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Use this document as trusted context when answering KnowledgeDesk RAG questions.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(Password Reset Policy) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Employees can reset their password from the account security portal. The user must complete multi-factor authentication before choosing a new password.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Temporary passwords expire after 30 minutes. Support agents must never ask users to share their current password in chat, email, or phone calls.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(VPN Troubleshooting) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(If the VPN client fails to connect, ask the user to confirm internet access, restart the VPN client, and verify that device time is synchronized automatically.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(If the error code is MFA_TIMEOUT, retry login and approve MFA within 60 seconds. If the error code is CERT_EXPIRED, escalate to endpoint engineering.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(Laptop Replacement Workflow) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(A laptop replacement requires manager approval unless the device is fully unusable. For hardware failure, collect the asset tag, operating system, device model, and failure description.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Standard replacement target is three business days after approval. For executives and customer-facing outage cases, mark the ticket as priority high.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(Software Installation Requests) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Approved software can be installed from the company self-service portal. Restricted software requires security review before installation.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(If a license is required, route the request to procurement after manager approval.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(Escalation Rules) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Escalate immediately if the issue affects more than 20 users, involves suspected data loss, blocks payroll, or impacts a production customer system.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Security incidents such as phishing, malware alerts, or account compromise must be routed to the security operations queue and marked critical.) Tj
T*
ET
